PHASE B: EXTENDED SCHEMA (21 TABLES), CONSTRAINTS, VIEWS, TRIGGERS, INDEXES, PROCEDURES
======================================================
Keep the 10 core tables exactly as in the project document (ITEM, SUPPLIER, PINCODE_CITY, SUPPLIER_CONTACT, DEPARTMENT, STOCK_BATCH, CONSUMABLE_ITEM, DURABLE_ITEM, SUPPLIES with surrogate PurchaseID, ISSUED_TO with surrogate IssueID). StockQty stays a DERIVED value, never a stored column.

B1. Add 11 extension tables (all in 3NF, ideally BCNF; write the FDs for each table in src/db/fds.ts so the Normalization lab can verify them):
- EMPLOYEE(EmpID PK, EmpName NOT NULL, Designation NOT NULL, DeptID FK NOT NULL, ManagerID FK to EMPLOYEE NULL [self-reference], Email UNIQUE, Phone)
- ROLE(RoleName PK, Description)
- PERMISSION(RoleName FK, Resource, Action, PK = all three)  [Action IN ('READ','CREATE','UPDATE','DELETE','APPROVE','FULFIL','EXPORT')]
- APP_USER(UserID PK, Username UNIQUE, PasswordHash, Salt, RoleName FK, EmpID FK UNIQUE)
- REQUISITION(ReqID PK, DeptID FK, EmpID FK, ReqDate, Status CHECK IN ('DRAFT','SUBMITTED','APPROVED','REJECTED','PARTIALLY_FULFILLED','FULFILLED'), ApprovedBy FK to APP_USER NULL, Remarks)
- REQUISITION_LINE(ReqID FK, LineNo, ItemID FK, QtyRequested CHECK > 0, QtyApproved NULL, PK = (ReqID, LineNo))  [a second weak entity, ON DELETE CASCADE from REQUISITION]
- AUDIT_LOG(AuditID INTEGER PK AUTOINCREMENT, TableName, RecordKey, Action CHECK IN ('INSERT','UPDATE','DELETE'), OldValues JSON text, NewValues JSON text, ChangedBy, ChangedAt)
- ALERT(AlertID PK, ItemID FK, AlertType CHECK IN ('LOW_STOCK','OUT_OF_STOCK','EXPIRING','PRICE_VARIANCE'), Message, CreatedAt, ResolvedAt NULL)
- PRICE_HISTORY(ItemID FK, ChangedAt, OldPrice, NewPrice, ChangedBy, PK = (ItemID, ChangedAt))
- PROCEDURE_REGISTRY(ProcName PK, ParamsJson, BodySql, Description)  [emulated stored procedures, see B6]
- SESSION_CONTEXT(Key PK, Value)  [emulates SESSION_USER()/session variables so triggers know the current app user and department; the app sets 'user', 'role', 'dept' at the start of every write transaction]
B2. Constraints (use real CHECK, NOT NULL, UNIQUE, FOREIGN KEY with ON DELETE RESTRICT/CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE where sensible): Quantity > 0; Cost >= 0; UnitPrice >= 0; WarrantyPeriod >= 0 (0 = no warranty); ReorderLevel >= 0; IssueDate and PurchaseDate not in the future (CHECK date(x) <= date('now')); ISSUED_TO.DeptID NOT NULL, EmpID nullable (and when present the employee must belong to that department, enforced by a trigger).
B3. Views (the UI reads these; each view is shown with its SQL in the Lab):
- V_CURRENT_STOCK: one row per item with TotalPurchased, TotalIssued, StockQty (derived), ItemType, ReorderLevel, WarrantyPeriod, status. Reference definition:
    CREATE VIEW V_CURRENT_STOCK AS
    SELECT i.ItemID, i.ItemName, i.Category, i.UnitPrice,
           COALESCE((SELECT SUM(Quantity) FROM SUPPLIES s WHERE s.ItemID = i.ItemID), 0) AS TotalPurchased,
           COALESCE((SELECT SUM(Quantity) FROM ISSUED_TO t WHERE t.ItemID = i.ItemID), 0) AS TotalIssued,
           COALESCE((SELECT SUM(Quantity) FROM SUPPLIES s WHERE s.ItemID = i.ItemID), 0)
         - COALESCE((SELECT SUM(Quantity) FROM ISSUED_TO t WHERE t.ItemID = i.ItemID), 0) AS StockQty,
           c.ReorderLevel, d.WarrantyPeriod,
           CASE WHEN c.ItemID IS NOT NULL THEN 'Consumable' ELSE 'Durable' END AS ItemType
    FROM ITEM i
    LEFT JOIN CONSUMABLE_ITEM c ON c.ItemID = i.ItemID
    LEFT JOIN DURABLE_ITEM d ON d.ItemID = i.ItemID;
- V_STOCK_LEDGER: UNION ALL of purchases (IN, positive) and issues (OUT, negative) with a running balance using a window function:
    SUM(Qty) OVER (PARTITION BY ItemID ORDER BY TxnDate, TxnType, Ref ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS RunningBalance
- V_LOW_STOCK, V_EXPIRING_BATCHES (next 30 days and already expired), V_DEPT_CONSUMPTION, V_SUPPLIER_SUMMARY, V_ITEM_FULL, V_REORDER_WORKLIST, and V_MY_DEPT_ISSUES (filters by (SELECT Value FROM SESSION_CONTEXT WHERE Key='dept'), showing a view used as a security layer).
B4. Triggers (real SQLite triggers, each listed in the Lab with a "Fire it" demo button):
- trg_issue_check_stock BEFORE INSERT ON ISSUED_TO:
    SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'INSUFFICIENT_STOCK') WHERE NEW.Quantity > (SELECT StockQty FROM V_CURRENT_STOCK WHERE ItemID = NEW.ItemID);
- trg_issue_emp_dept BEFORE INSERT ON ISSUED_TO: abort with 'EMPLOYEE_DEPT_MISMATCH' if EmpID is not NULL and that employee's DeptID differs from NEW.DeptID.
- trg_issue_alert AFTER INSERT ON ISSUED_TO: insert a LOW_STOCK or OUT_OF_STOCK row into ALERT when StockQty <= ReorderLevel and no unresolved alert exists for that item.
- trg_purchase_resolve_alert AFTER INSERT ON SUPPLIES: set ResolvedAt on open stock alerts for the item once StockQty > ReorderLevel.
- trg_supplies_delete_guard BEFORE DELETE ON SUPPLIES: abort with 'NEGATIVE_STOCK_GUARD' if removing it would make stock negative (same check for BEFORE UPDATE OF Quantity).
- trg_price_history AFTER UPDATE OF UnitPrice ON ITEM: insert into PRICE_HISTORY.
- trg_price_variance AFTER INSERT ON SUPPLIES: insert a PRICE_VARIANCE alert when Cost / Quantity is more than 15% above ITEM.UnitPrice.
- trg_disjoint_consumable BEFORE INSERT ON CONSUMABLE_ITEM: SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'DISJOINT_VIOLATION') WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM DURABLE_ITEM WHERE ItemID = NEW.ItemID); and the mirror trigger on DURABLE_ITEM. (Enforces the disjoint "d" specialization from the EER diagram. Total participation is checked by sp_add_item and by a self-test.)
- Audit triggers AFTER INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on ITEM, SUPPLIER, SUPPLIES, ISSUED_TO, DEPARTMENT, REQUISITION writing json_object(...) of old and new values plus (SELECT Value FROM SESSION_CONTEXT WHERE Key='user') and datetime('now') into AUDIT_LOG.
B5. Indexes (documented with the query each one serves): idx_supplies_item_date(ItemID, PurchaseDate), idx_issued_item_date(ItemID, IssueDate), idx_issued_dept_date(DeptID, IssueDate), idx_item_category(Category), idx_item_name(ItemName COLLATE NOCASE), idx_audit_table_key(TableName, RecordKey), idx_alert_open(ItemID) WHERE ResolvedAt IS NULL (a partial index), idx_req_status(Status).
B6. Stored procedures are EMULATED (SQLite has none): a procedure registry of named parameterized scripts executed by the worker inside one transaction. Required: sp_add_item, sp_record_purchase, sp_issue_item, sp_submit_requisition, sp_approve_requisition, sp_fulfil_requisition (see D2, uses SAVEPOINT per line), sp_reset_demo. Every procedure sets SESSION_CONTEXT first, checks PERMISSION, runs its statements, and on any error does ROLLBACK and returns { ok:false, code, message }.
B7. Error codes: map RAISE messages and SQLite errors to friendly clay toasts and inline form errors: INSUFFICIENT_STOCK ("Only X units available" with a "Reduce to X" button), NEGATIVE_STOCK_GUARD, DISJOINT_VIOLATION, EMPLOYEE_DEPT_MISMATCH, UNIQUE constraint, "FOREIGN KEY constraint failed" (explain which referencing table blocks the delete, using PRAGMA foreign_key_list), CHECK constraint failed.

