PHASE E: THE DATABASE LAB (the main differentiator)
======================================================
Turn the Database Lab into a tabbed workspace. Each tab is lazy-loaded.
E1. Live Schema Browser: built from introspect() (sqlite_master, PRAGMA table_info, foreign_key_list, index_list), NOT hardcoded. Interactive relationship graph with PK/FK icons, a row-count badge per table, DDL viewer, and first rows. Keep the hand-drawn EER diagram as its own tab (strong and weak entities, double diamond identifying relationship, multivalued Contact, composite Address, derived StockQty, disjoint Is-a with Consumable and Durable), and extend it with the new entities.
E2. SQL Workbench: a SQL editor (lightweight, lazy-loaded; syntax highlighting, Ctrl+Enter to run, query history, saved queries). Modes: "Read-only (main DB)" by default, which blocks writes with PRAGMA query_only = ON; and "Sandbox (writes allowed)", which runs against a disposable clone, with a visible banner and a "Discard sandbox" button. Result tabs: Results (virtualized grid, CSV export), Plan (EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN rendered as a tree with SCAN vs SEARCH highlighted and "USING INDEX" or "COVERING INDEX" badges), Timing, and Relational Algebra (see E6).
E3. Query Library: 40 curated queries on the stationery data, each with: title, the business question, SQL, concept tags, the relational algebra expression, expected insight, and a "Run" and "Open in Workbench" button. Required coverage (minimum counts): selection and projection (3); joins including INNER, LEFT, CROSS and a SELF-JOIN on EMPLOYEE manager (6); GROUP BY, HAVING and aggregates (5); subqueries including scalar, IN, EXISTS, NOT EXISTS and correlated (6); set operations UNION, INTERSECT, EXCEPT (3); window functions RANK, DENSE_RANK, ROW_NUMBER, LAG/LEAD, NTILE and running totals (6); CTEs including a RECURSIVE CTE for the 12-month series with zero-fill and another for the approval chain of command up the manager hierarchy (4); views (3); CASE and date functions (3); JSON functions on AUDIT_LOG (2); and one RELATIONAL DIVISION query ("departments that have been issued items from EVERY category", written with double NOT EXISTS). Reference for the 12-month series:
    WITH RECURSIVE months(m) AS (
      SELECT date('now','start of month','-11 months')
      UNION ALL SELECT date(m,'+1 month') FROM months WHERE m < date('now','start of month'))
    SELECT m, COALESCE(SUM(t.Quantity),0) AS Issued
    FROM months LEFT JOIN ISSUED_TO t ON strftime('%Y-%m', t.IssueDate) = strftime('%Y-%m', m)
    GROUP BY m ORDER BY m;
E4. Index and Optimizer Lab: a "Generate 50,000 transactions" button that creates a SANDBOX database (never the main one) via a recursive-CTE bulk insert, WITHOUT the secondary indexes. Guided steps: run a query (for example total issued per item in a date range) and show EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN as SCAN plus timing; click "CREATE INDEX idx_issued_item_date"; rerun and show SEARCH USING INDEX (or COVERING INDEX) plus the new timing with a before/after bar chart and the percentage improvement. Also demonstrate a composite index column-order effect, a partial index, and a case where an index is NOT used (function on the column) with the reason. Destroy the sandbox on exit.
